# freezed / json_serializable output (composed lib/ output is covered by the
# lib/ rule below; this catches strays elsewhere). integration_test's
# tour_steps.g.dart is deliberately force-tracked, supacharge-style, so the
# guided-tour runner compiles outside CI too.
*.freezed.dart
*.g.dart

# --- Composed app shell (supacharge pattern) ---
# Compose/install machinery cache and machine-local overrides.
.rokct/cache/
.rokct/__pycache__/
.rokct/win_dev_overrides/
# Machine-local dependency overrides. `dart pub` merges pubspec_overrides.yaml
# over pubspec.yaml's dependency_overrides automatically, so dev-machine
# workarounds belong there - never in the tracked pubspec.yaml, which is what
# CI resolves.
pubspec_overrides.yaml
# lib/ is generated by compose on every build - main.dart included - so
# none of it is tracked and a fresh checkout regenerates it. Everything
# app-specific that used to be hand-written there now lives in manifest data
# (radio_sdk's routes/boot hooks, host_routes in composer.json) and in
# build config (dart-defines) - which IS tracked and is the real source of
# truth. The pre-slice originals are preserved under docs/legacy/lib/.
lib/
# assets/ is deliberately NOT ignored: installed assets (assets/radio/ from
# radio_sdk, splash, brand images) are tracked so this shell repo owns and
# can rebrand them. The SDK installer's hash-guard skips any asset a
# developer has modified (or that it has no record of installing), so
# rebranded files survive recompose.
